  ($qb$ITEM-SJT-1174$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$A team spends ten minutes at the start of every weekly meeting collecting figures that are already available in a live dashboard. What do you do?$qb$, $qb$Propose that participants review the dashboard before or during the meeting and use the saved time for exceptions, decisions and actions that require discussion.$qb$, $qb$Keep collecting figures because it ensures everyone hears the same numbers.$qb$, $qb$Cancel the weekly meeting entirely.$qb$, $qb$Ask one person to read the dashboard figures aloud faster.$qb$, $qb$Send screenshots before the meeting but still repeat the collection.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-SJT-118$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$A frequently used internal guide is outdated and causes repeated questions. You are not the document owner, but you know what needs updating. What do you do?$qb$, $qb$Confirm the changes with the owner, prepare a clear update or evidence, and help get the guide corrected through the proper process.$qb$, $qb$Create your own updated copy and share it with your team.$qb$, $qb$Tell coworkers the guide is outdated whenever questions arise.$qb$, $qb$Wait for the owner to notice.$qb$, $qb$Replace the official file without telling the owner.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-SJT-1450$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$A team spends time each week manually reminding owners about actions already showing overdue alerts in the shared system. What do you do?$qb$, $qb$Use the system's overdue alerts as the default and spend human effort only on exceptions or escalations the alerts do not resolve.$qb$, $qb$Keep manual reminders because they are more personal.$qb$, $qb$Rotate reminder duty.$qb$, $qb$Send more reminders to ensure action.$qb$, $qb$Turn off the system alerts and keep the manual process.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-SJT-1588$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$A recurring update requires someone to manually copy the same deadline dates from the project plan into an email every Monday. What do you do?$qb$, $qb$Use an approved shared view or generated update from the project plan so dates are maintained once, with manual commentary only where needed.$qb$, $qb$Create an email template and keep copying dates.$qb$, $qb$Rotate the task weekly.$qb$, $qb$Stop sending the update.$qb$, $qb$Ask recipients to open the project plan without checking whether they need commentary.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-SJT-162$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You finish your assigned work earlier than expected and notice a recurring team problem that nobody currently owns. What do you do?$qb$, $qb$Confirm the problem is worth solving, take a manageable first step to understand or improve it, and involve the right people before changing shared work.$qb$, $qb$Tell your manager you have spare capacity and suggest the problem as a possible next task.$qb$, $qb$Create a workaround that reduces the problem for your own work.$qb$, $qb$Use the extra time to polish work that already meets the required standard.$qb$, $qb$Wait for another assignment because taking on unassigned problems can interfere with priorities.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
