  ($qb$ITEM-SJT-438$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You notice that a routine weekly request requires people to ask the same person for a file that could safely be stored in a shared location. What do you do?$qb$, $qb$Confirm the file can be shared under existing access rules, propose an authoritative shared location and update ownership, and test whether it removes repeated requests.$qb$, $qb$Upload your copy to a shared folder and tell people where it is.$qb$, $qb$Keep requesting the file because the current owner may have reasons for controlling it.$qb$, $qb$Tell the file owner that people are wasting time and wait for them to change the process.$qb$, $qb$Create an unofficial copy that your immediate team can reuse.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
