  ($qb$ITEM-SJT-803$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$During an incident, a senior colleague strongly suggests a fix you believe could make the problem worse. Time is short. What do you do?$qb$, $qb$State the specific risk calmly, check the quickest relevant evidence, and propose a safer reversible step or condition for trying the fix rather than yielding to status pressure.$qb$, $qb$Follow the senior colleague because they have more experience.$qb$, $qb$Refuse the fix without offering an alternative.$qb$, $qb$Ask management to decide before anyone acts.$qb$, $qb$Try the fix immediately and reverse it if things worsen.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
