  ($qb$HEAIL-RES-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a small shop. Takings have fallen for four months running. You have tried two promotions and neither made a difference. Your savings will cover about six more months. How do you proceed?$qb$, $qb$Find out why customers are not coming before spending anything more$qb$, $qb$Try a different kind of promotion from the two that failed$qb$, $qb$Cut costs so the six months stretches further$qb$, $qb$Keep going, since trade may pick up in the new season$qb$, $qb$Close now while the savings are still intact$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
