  ($qb$HEAIL-RES-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a salesperson. You have had no sales for six weeks in a role where two a week is normal. Your manager has not raised it. How do you handle this?$qb$, $qb$Take your recent calls to your manager and ask what she would change$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager for a review of how you are working$qb$, $qb$Work out yourself what has changed in the last six weeks$qb$, $qb$Increase the number of calls you make each day$qb$, $qb$Wait, since sales roles have quiet periods$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-RES-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a student on a work placement. Three weeks in, you are finding the work much harder than expected and are behind the other placement students. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell your supervisor where you are struggling and ask what to focus on$qb$, $qb$Ask one of the other students how they are approaching the work$qb$, $qb$Put in extra hours until you have caught up with the others$qb$, $qb$Keep going quietly, since admitting it may count against you$qb$, $qb$Ask to be moved to easier work for the rest of the placement$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-RES-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a small team. A member who is usually reliable has made three errors this fortnight and seems flat. You do not know why. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Ask him how things are going before raising the errors$qb$, $qb$Raise the errors with him and ask whether something has changed$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague whether they have noticed anything$qb$, $qb$Watch for another week before saying anything$qb$, $qb$Raise the errors as a performance matter and leave it there$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-RES-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a mechanic. A car has come back three times with the same fault, and you have not found the cause. The customer is losing patience. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell the customer where you have got to and bring in a second opinion$qb$, $qb$Tell the customer you have not found it and are still looking$qb$, $qb$Start again from the beginning rather than repeat your checks$qb$, $qb$Try one more thing before saying anything to the customer$qb$, $qb$Tell the customer to take it to a main dealer instead$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-RES-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a teacher in your first year. A class you teach has been difficult all term and you dread the lesson. Other teachers manage the same class. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask one of them to watch your lesson and tell you what they see$qb$, $qb$Ask them what they do differently with that class$qb$, $qb$Try a different approach with the class next lesson$qb$, $qb$Keep going, since first-year teachers often struggle$qb$, $qb$Ask for the class to be reassigned to someone else$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-RES-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a warehouse. You have applied for a supervisor role twice and been turned down twice. A third round opens in six months. How do you use the time?$qb$, $qb$Ask what was missing both times, and work on that specifically$qb$, $qb$Ask for feedback on the second application$qb$, $qb$Take on extra responsibility so your application is stronger$qb$, $qb$Apply again and hope the third time is different$qb$, $qb$Look for a supervisor role at another company instead$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-RES-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a self-employed decorator. A large job you were counting on has been cancelled with no notice. You have two weeks of work booked after that. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Start filling the gap today, and ask why the job was cancelled$qb$, $qb$Start looking for work to fill the two weeks straight away$qb$, $qb$Ask the client whether any part of the job could still go ahead$qb$, $qb$Use the free time to catch up on other things$qb$, $qb$Wait to see whether the client changes their mind$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-RES-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are an office worker. A system change has made your job noticeably harder and slower. Two months in, you are still slower than before. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Show your manager where the time is going and ask what can change$qb$, $qb$Tell your manager the new system is slowing you down$qb$, $qb$Ask colleagues whether they have found ways around it$qb$, $qb$Keep going, since you will get faster with practice$qb$, $qb$Go back to doing it the old way where you can$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-RES-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a chef. A dish you developed has been on the menu for a month and barely sells. You believe it is good. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Find out why it is not selling before deciding what to do$qb$, $qb$Change the dish based on what customers have said$qb$, $qb$Give it another month before making any decision$qb$, $qb$Keep it on, since you believe in the dish$qb$, $qb$Take it off the menu and move on to something else$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-RES-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You lead a small charity project. Funding has been refused twice and your volunteers are losing heart. There is one more funder to approach. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell the volunteers where things stand and what the last application needs$qb$, $qb$Tell the volunteers there is one more funder to try$qb$, $qb$Make the third application before saying anything to them$qb$, $qb$Tell them things are still going well so they do not give up$qb$, $qb$Tell them the project will probably not go ahead$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-RES-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a carer for a demanding client. The work has been getting harder for months and you have started dreading the visits. The client's needs have not changed. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell your supervisor how the visits have become for you$qb$, $qb$Ask your supervisor whether the visits could be shared$qb$, $qb$Work out what specifically has become difficult about them$qb$, $qb$Keep going, since the client depends on you$qb$, $qb$Ask to be taken off the client's visits$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
