  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-FIB-012$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A course attended and never applied has to be paid for twice, once in the time and once in the ______.$qb$, $qb$relearning$qb$, $qb$booking$qb$, $qb$travel$qb$, $qb$paperwork$qb$, $qb$feedback$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-FIB-013$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Someone who explains their reasoning teaches you more than someone who gives you the ______.$qb$, $qb$answer$qb$, $qb$task$qb$, $qb$warning$qb$, $qb$outcome$qb$, $qb$instruction$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A new skill is easiest to keep when it is used in the ______ that follows the training.$qb$, $qb$week$qb$, $qb$time$qb$, $qb$meeting$qb$, $qb$report$qb$, $qb$interview$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Someone who can say where their new skill stops has a more useful grasp of its ______.$qb$, $qb$limits$qb$, $qb$history$qb$, $qb$cost$qb$, $qb$popularity$qb$, $qb$wording$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-017$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have been sent on a one-day training course. What is most likely to make it useful?$qb$, $qb$Using one thing from it in the following week$qb$, $qb$Taking detailed notes during the day$qb$, $qb$Asking questions about the parts you find unclear$qb$, $qb$Reviewing your notes soon after the course$qb$, $qb$Sharing what you learned with your team$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want to learn a skill that nobody in your team has. What is the best first step?$qb$, $qb$Find someone outside the team who already does it$qb$, $qb$Look for training your employer would fund$qb$, $qb$Read about it and start practising on your own$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager whether it would be useful$qb$, $qb$Wait until the skill is actually needed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have been told something at work that does not match what you learned in training. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask what has changed since the training was written$qb$, $qb$Ask which of the two you should be following$qb$, $qb$Follow the workplace version, since it is current$qb$, $qb$Follow your training, since it was formally taught$qb$, $qb$Do it both ways and see which works better$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably turns something you have read about into something you can do?$qb$, $qb$Doing it where someone can correct you$qb$, $qb$Doing it several times on your own$qb$, $qb$Watching someone else do it first$qb$, $qb$Reading about it more thoroughly$qb$, $qb$Writing down the steps involved$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You do not understand something a colleague has explained twice. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say which part loses you and ask about that$qb$, $qb$Ask her to explain it a third time$qb$, $qb$Ask someone else to explain it instead$qb$, $qb$Say you understand and work it out later$qb$, $qb$Look it up yourself rather than ask again$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A younger colleague uses a tool you have never learned. What is the most useful response?$qb$, $qb$Ask her to show you what it does for her work$qb$, $qb$Ask her whether it would be useful for yours$qb$, $qb$Read about the tool in your own time$qb$, $qb$Continue with what you use, since it works$qb$, $qb$Ask whether training on it is available$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have three hours a month for learning. What is the best use of it?$qb$, $qb$One thing you will use in the work you already do$qb$, $qb$The area where you are furthest behind$qb$, $qb$Something that would help you get promoted$qb$, $qb$Whatever seems most interesting at the time$qb$, $qb$Reading widely so you know a bit of everything$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have learned a faster way to do part of your job. What is the most useful next step?$qb$, $qb$Show a colleague, so the method does not stay with you$qb$, $qb$Use it and see whether it holds up over time$qb$, $qb$Tell your manager that you have found it$qb$, $qb$Write it down for your own reference$qb$, $qb$Keep using it, since it works for you$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone senior has explained a decision using reasoning you do not follow. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask him to take you through the step you missed$qb$, $qb$Ask him to explain the decision again$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague afterwards what he meant$qb$, $qb$Accept the decision without following the reasoning$qb$, $qb$Look into the subject yourself afterwards$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually makes a mistake worth more than the trouble it caused?$qb$, $qb$Understanding the conditions that produced it$qb$, $qb$Making sure it does not happen again$qb$, $qb$Reporting it so others can learn from it$qb$, $qb$Correcting it quickly and completely$qb$, $qb$Accepting responsibility for having made it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
