  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague explains something to you in a way you find confusing. What is the most useful response?$qb$, $qb$Say back what you understood and ask what you missed$qb$, $qb$Ask her to explain it a different way$qb$, $qb$Ask her to slow down and go through it again$qb$, $qb$Thank her and work it out on your own$qb$, $qb$Ask a different colleague to explain it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want to understand how your work affects another department. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Spend an hour watching what they do with it$qb$, $qb$Ask them what problems your work causes them$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager how the two connect$qb$, $qb$Read the process documents for both$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague who has worked in both$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably shows that training has worked?$qb$, $qb$Something is being done differently afterwards$qb$, $qb$The people trained say it was useful$qb$, $qb$The people trained can explain the content$qb$, $qb$Attendance was good and questions were asked$qb$, $qb$The training was delivered as planned$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have been given feedback that you need to improve at something. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Find out what good looks like before practising$qb$, $qb$Practise it regularly until it improves$qb$, $qb$Ask for training in that area$qb$, $qb$Ask someone good at it to work alongside you$qb$, $qb$Focus on it more carefully in your daily work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a shop assistant. A customer has asked a detailed question about a product and you could not answer it. Your colleague answered it easily. How do you handle this?$qb$, $qb$Ask her how she knew, and find out what else you are missing$qb$, $qb$Ask her to explain that product to you properly$qb$, $qb$Read up on that product range in a quiet moment$qb$, $qb$Refer similar questions to her in future$qb$, $qb$Note that she knows the product better than you$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a nurse. A new piece of equipment has arrived on the ward. The formal training is next month, but two colleagues were shown it last week and it is in use now. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask an experienced colleague to guide you before your first use$qb$, $qb$Study the equipment manual carefully before using it yourself$qb$, $qb$Watch experienced colleagues use the equipment several times$qb$, $qb$Use the equipment cautiously and attend next month's training$qb$, $qb$Avoid the equipment completely until formal training is delivered$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
