  ($qb$HEAIL-CLC-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A6-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a teacher in your second year. A colleague's classes are noticeably better behaved than yours. She has not offered any advice. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Ask whether you can sit in on one of her lessons$qb$, $qb$Ask her what she does in the first ten minutes$qb$, $qb$Ask her for advice on managing your classes$qb$, $qb$Watch how she speaks to students in the corridor$qb$, $qb$Work on it yourself rather than admit the problem$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
