  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-FIB-011$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Working only while someone is watching means you never learn to work ______.$qb$, $qb$unsupervised$qb$, $qb$overtime$qb$, $qb$remotely$qb$, $qb$in pairs$qb$, $qb$jointly$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-FIB-012$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Boredom in a job is a signal to look for what nobody is ______.$qb$, $qb$doing$qb$, $qb$paying$qb$, $qb$watching$qb$, $qb$counting$qb$, $qb$reading$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-FIB-013$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A habit survives the day your enthusiasm ______.$qb$, $qb$fails$qb$, $qb$doubles$qb$, $qb$returns$qb$, $qb$spreads$qb$, $qb$arrives$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-FIB-014$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Someone who finishes what they start becomes the person others ______.$qb$, $qb$ask$qb$, $qb$wait for$qb$, $qb$brief$qb$, $qb$supervise$qb$, $qb$replace$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The gap between wanting to and beginning is where most plans ______.$qb$, $qb$die$qb$, $qb$slow$qb$, $qb$double$qb$, $qb$spread$qb$, $qb$multiply$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A person who solves a problem nobody assigned them has just shown what they can ______.$qb$, $qb$do$qb$, $qb$sell$qb$, $qb$spend$qb$, $qb$carry$qb$, $qb$store$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-FIB-017$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Small progress recorded daily outlasts a large effort made ______.$qb$, $qb$once$qb$, $qb$publicly$qb$, $qb$cheaply$qb$, $qb$jointly$qb$, $qb$seasonally$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have finished your work and nobody has given you anything else. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Find something that needed doing and start it$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager what else needs doing$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague whether they need help$qb$, $qb$Use the time to tidy your own area$qb$, $qb$Wait until you are given something$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have an idea for improving your work but no authority to change anything. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Try it on the part you do control and show the result$qb$, $qb$Put the idea to whoever can approve it$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague whether the idea would work$qb$, $qb$Wait for a suitable moment to raise it$qb$, $qb$Drop it, since you cannot make the change$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably keeps someone going on a long piece of work?$qb$, $qb$Seeing that the work has moved each day$qb$, $qb$Remembering why the work matters$qb$, $qb$Having a deadline to work towards$qb$, $qb$Being checked on regularly$qb$, $qb$Enjoying the work itself$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want to learn something that would help your work. Nobody will pay for training. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Find the part you can learn by doing and start there$qb$, $qb$Ask whether training could be funded later$qb$, $qb$Find out what the training would cost$qb$, $qb$Ask someone who already has the skill to show you$qb$, $qb$Wait until training becomes available$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually happens to a plan that exists only in someone's head?$qb$, $qb$It is quietly abandoned without anyone noticing$qb$, $qb$It takes longer than planned$qb$, $qb$It changes without being decided$qb$, $qb$It is forgotten in the detail$qb$, $qb$It never gets the resources it needs$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A task you dislike has been sitting on your list for a week. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Do the first ten minutes of it now$qb$, $qb$Schedule a time to do it properly$qb$, $qb$Break it into smaller pieces$qb$, $qb$Do it when you feel more like it$qb$, $qb$Ask whether someone else could take it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have noticed something going wrong in another part of the business. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Tell whoever can act, with what you have seen$qb$, $qb$Mention it to your own manager$qb$, $qb$Find out more before saying anything$qb$, $qb$Wait to see whether someone else raises it$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since it is not your area$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the main difference between someone who waits and someone who starts?$qb$, $qb$The one who starts finds out what the work involves$qb$, $qb$Starting brings the finish date closer$qb$, $qb$Waiting can avoid effort spent on the wrong thing$qb$, $qb$Beginning early carries more risk of wasted work$qb$, $qb$Delay allows more information to arrive$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are offered a piece of work you are not sure you can do. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Take it and be clear about what you will need$qb$, $qb$Take it and work out the difficulties as you go$qb$, $qb$Ask what support would be available first$qb$, $qb$Ask for time to think about it$qb$, $qb$Decline, since you are not sure you can do it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your enthusiasm for a project has faded halfway through. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Set a small piece you can finish this week$qb$, $qb$Remind yourself why you started it$qb$, $qb$Take a break and return to it$qb$, $qb$Ask someone to work on it with you$qb$, $qb$Push on until the feeling returns$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably turns an intention into something that actually happens?$qb$, $qb$Deciding when and where you will do it$qb$, $qb$Setting a deadline for it$qb$, $qb$Writing the intention down$qb$, $qb$Telling someone you intend to do it$qb$, $qb$Making a plan for how to do it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have spotted a small job that would help everyone but belongs to nobody. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Do it and tell the team it is done$qb$, $qb$Suggest it at the next team meeting$qb$, $qb$Do it quietly without mentioning it$qb$, $qb$Ask who ought to be doing it$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since it belongs to nobody$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually limits someone who only works when they are supervised?$qb$, $qb$They never find out what they would choose to do$qb$, $qb$They do less work than others$qb$, $qb$They are given less responsibility$qb$, $qb$Their work needs more checking$qb$, $qb$They are seen as less reliable$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want more responsible work but have not been offered any. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Take on a piece of it and do it well$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager for more responsibility$qb$, $qb$Ask what would make you ready for it$qb$, $qb$Wait until your work is noticed$qb$, $qb$Apply for a role elsewhere$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the main value of finishing something small today rather than planning something large?$qb$, $qb$You learn something the plan could not tell you$qb$, $qb$You feel better about the day$qb$, $qb$The small thing is done$qb$, $qb$You avoid over-planning$qb$, $qb$You can plan better afterwards$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A project you volunteered for has turned out to be much bigger than expected. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say what you can complete and by when$qb$, $qb$Ask for help with the extra work$qb$, $qb$Carry on and take longer over it$qb$, $qb$Ask whether the project can be reduced$qb$, $qb$Hand it back, since it was not what you agreed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably shows that someone will finish what they start?$qb$, $qb$They have finished things before$qb$, $qb$They plan the work carefully$qb$, $qb$They ask good questions about it$qb$, $qb$They are enthusiastic at the start$qb$, $qb$They say they will finish it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have been given a dull task that will take all week. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find the part of it that teaches you something$qb$, $qb$Work out how to do it faster$qb$, $qb$Set yourself a target for each day$qb$, $qb$Do it early each morning to get it over with$qb$, $qb$Ask whether it could be shared$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually happens when someone waits for the right conditions to start?$qb$, $qb$The conditions rarely arrive on their own$qb$, $qb$The work becomes harder to start$qb$, $qb$Someone else starts it first$qb$, $qb$The opportunity passes$qb$, $qb$They lose interest in the work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work on a seed sorting floor. Your shift finishes an hour early most days because the supply runs out. Nobody has given you anything for that hour. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Find something in the unit that needs doing and start it$qb$, $qb$Ask the supervisor what to do with the hour$qb$, $qb$Ask other workers whether they need help$qb$, $qb$Clean and tidy your own station$qb$, $qb$Wait, since you have finished what you were given$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work at a tempo loading point. You have noticed that loads are packed in an order that makes unloading slow, but the order is not yours to set. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Pack one load differently and show what it saved at unloading$qb$, $qb$Suggest the change to whoever sets the order$qb$, $qb$Ask the drivers whether they find unloading slow$qb$, $qb$Mention it if anyone asks about unloading times$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the order is not yours to change$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a lift operator in an old building. The job leaves you with long idle periods and you have started to find the days very long. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Find something useful you can do between calls and start doing it$qb$, $qb$Ask the building manager for extra duties$qb$, $qb$Ask other staff whether they need help$qb$, $qb$Use the time to rest for the busy periods$qb$, $qb$Accept it, since the job is what it is$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work a hostel mess counter. You would like to learn the kitchen work but there is no training and the cook is always busy. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Learn one step by watching and doing it when the counter is quiet$qb$, $qb$Ask the cook to teach you when he has time$qb$, $qb$Ask the warden whether training is possible$qb$, $qb$Watch the cook whenever you can$qb$, $qb$Wait until a kitchen place becomes available$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a cane crusher yard. You have an idea that would reduce spillage but the yard layout is decided by the owner, who visits monthly. How do you proceed?$qb$, $qb$Try it on your own section and record what changes$qb$, $qb$Put the idea to the owner at his next visit$qb$, $qb$Ask the other workers whether they agree with it$qb$, $qb$Wait for the owner's visit to raise it$qb$, $qb$Drop it, since the layout is not yours to change$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work at an oil expeller unit. You have finished your allotted sacks and there are two hours left. The supervisor has gone for the day. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Start on what will be needed tomorrow and leave a note$qb$, $qb$Ask another worker what needs doing$qb$, $qb$Clean and prepare your machine for tomorrow$qb$, $qb$Wait for the supervisor to return$qb$, $qb$Leave, since your sacks are finished$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You sort files at a records desk. You have noticed that one kind of request always takes twice as long and you think you know why. Nobody has asked you. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Change how you handle those requests and see whether it holds$qb$, $qb$Tell your supervisor what you have noticed$qb$, $qb$Time the requests properly first$qb$, $qb$Mention it if the delay is ever raised$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since nobody has asked$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work at a cinema ticket window. Sales have fallen and you have an idea for a change to the opening hours. You have no authority over hours. How do you proceed?$qb$, $qb$Record the arrivals you see outside opening hours and take that in$qb$, $qb$Suggest the change to the manager$qb$, $qb$Ask customers whether different hours would suit them$qb$, $qb$Ask colleagues whether they agree with the idea$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since hours are set above you$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work on a sweet packing table. Your target is met by two in the afternoon and the remaining time is unstructured. You have done this for a month. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Use the afternoons to learn the next stage of the work$qb$, $qb$Ask the supervisor for a higher target$qb$, $qb$Help others who are behind on their targets$qb$, $qb$Work more slowly so the day is filled$qb$, $qb$Take the afternoons easy, since the target is met$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You clean night buses. A cleaner on the other shift always leaves the rear section undone and you have been doing it. Nobody has noticed. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Raise it now with the person who sets the shifts$qb$, $qb$Speak to the other cleaner about the rear section$qb$, $qb$Keep doing it and mention it if asked$qb$, $qb$Leave the rear section undone so it becomes visible$qb$, $qb$Keep doing it, since the buses get cleaned$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a pipe threading shop as an employee. A customer has asked for something the shop does not offer, and you can see three more could want it. The owner is away. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Work out what it would take and have it ready for the owner's return$qb$, $qb$Phone the owner to ask whether to take it on$qb$, $qb$Tell the customer to come back when the owner returns$qb$, $qb$Take the job and tell the owner afterwards$qb$, $qb$Turn the customer away, since the shop does not offer it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work at a bangle polishing bench. You want to move to the design side but there is no route from one to the other in your unit. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Learn what you can from the designers and produce something to show$qb$, $qb$Ask the owner whether a move would be possible$qb$, $qb$Ask a designer to teach you in your own time$qb$, $qb$Wait for a vacancy on the design side$qb$, $qb$Accept that the two sides are separate$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a cattle fodder shop for the owner. Trade is slow in the afternoons and the owner has not raised it. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Try one change in the afternoon and see what it does to takings$qb$, $qb$Tell the owner that afternoons are slow$qb$, $qb$Ask customers why they come in the morning$qb$, $qb$Reduce afternoon staffing to save cost$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the owner has not raised it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SME-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You sell brooms and baskets door to door on a fixed round. A new housing block has been built on your route and nobody there knows you exist. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Start working the block and let the first customers bring the others$qb$, $qb$Leave a note at each door explaining what you do$qb$, $qb$Ask a resident to mention you to the others$qb$, $qb$Wait until someone from the block stops you on the round$qb$, $qb$Keep to your usual route, since it is established$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true)
